                <pb facs="0221" n="85" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg85"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15/872: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chairman of the American Delegation</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Gibson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-04-15T16:00:00+01:00">April 15, 1929—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 15—11:15 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>2. Preparatory Commission met this morning and after president had made rather
                    innocuous speech he submitted a proposed agenda which is substantially the
                    Colban proposal slightly elaborated.</p>
                <p>This will be discussed at tomorrow morning’s meeting.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gibson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
